Q: How to close Bootstrap info using click event in Angular 18 A: <ol>
<li>to show it on click/manually, disable triggers <code>triggers=&quot;&quot;</code></li>
</ol>
<pre><code>&lt;button
  class=&quot;sr-info-icon-set sr-info-control&quot;
  style=&quot;margin: auto;&quot;
  [tooltip]=&quot;staticHtmlTooltip&quot;
  container=&quot;body&quot;
  placement=&quot;auto&quot;
  (click)=&quot;toggleTooltip()&quot;
  triggers=&quot;&quot;
&gt;
  Info
&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<ol start="2">
<li>clicks from tooltip are disabled by default, enable pointer events to enable them:</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>.tooltip-content {
  text-align: left;
  color: whitesmoke;
  padding: 15px;
  width: 150px;
  height: 150px;
  pointer-events: auto;
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/ngx-bootstrap-example-r4vvq2gy?file=app%2Fapp.component.css" rel="nofollow noreferrer">demo</a></p>
